15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Schematic figure with two panels. Panel A shows characteristics of a candidate stem-like CD4-positive T cell, highlighting surface markers PD-1, SLAMF6, and IL-7R, core transcription factors TCF1 and context-dependent BCL6, limited terminal lineage commitment, and features in mouse and human. Panel B displays a transcriptional program diagram with branches for progenitor-associated and effector-differentiation modules; TCF1 and BCL6 promote progenitor maintenance, while PRDM1/BLIMP-1, IRF4, and LDHA drive effector differentiation and transition, with regulatory arrows and inhibition lines. Population-level evidence icons for persistence, multilineage output, and effector potential are included.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Infographic describing determinants of TCF1-positive PD-1-negative CD4-positive T-cell fate, showing three panels: spatial fate context, immunological constraints, and time-dependent metabolic effects, with labeled diagrams and key steps influencing effector and regulatory T-cell outcomes in the tumor environment.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Infographic depicting four strategies for achieving therapeutic balance in antitumor immunity: A\) Release constraints by blocking immune inhibitors, B\) Preserve precursor pool using cytokines and metabolic modulation, C\) Drive effector output through IL-12 and glycolysis, and D\) Engineer cell products using ACT and gene editing. Central image shows a scale balancing candidate precursor pool and productive effectors, leading to durable antitumor immunity emphasizing persistence, function, and safety. Icons represent cells, molecular pathways, and medical interventions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
